-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), G.N. No. S 914/2021, current version as at 5 November 2026.
-- roc8: ORDERS 34 TO 38 (arbitral proceedings, Bills of Sale Act, Building and Construction
-- Industry Security of Payment Act, Choice of Court Agreements Act, Companies Act).
-- NOUNS shared by the five Order modules of roc8: DECLARE only, no rules, no #EVAL.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore Statutes Online.
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here has been checked against the official text.
--
-- Every type and constructor begins with the label of the first rule that needs it, as
-- PLAN.md section 1 requires, so that no other part can declare the same name.

-- The ways the Orders say an application is made.  O 34 r 2 and r 3 name the first four;
-- O 38 r 2(3) names an originating claim.  `in some other way` is how a case the Orders do not
-- name is asked about: no rule answers JUST TRUE for it.
DECLARE `o 34 r 2 way an application is made` IS ONE OF
    `o 34 r 2 by originating application`
    `o 34 r 2 by originating application without notice`
    `o 34 r 2 by summons in the action`
    `o 34 r 2 by summons without notice`
    `o 34 r 2 by originating claim`
    `o 34 r 2 in some other way`
